{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Advantages to Cloud Computing"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use when talking about benefits of using cloud services. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.  Interpret the IT needs assessment, to determine the required technology to manage information, according to the rules and protocols established by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Be Supposed to in Affirmative and Negative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong>Be supposed to</strong> is used when you want to talk about things that you assume are going to be done by an agent.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>In general, <strong>be supposed to</strong> is used when we imply expectation:</p> <p>For example:</p> <p><i>I&rsquo;m going to use cloud services. They<strong> are supposed to be</strong> effective.</i></p> <p>Here, the person who speaks expect cloud services to be effective.</p> <p><strong><i>I am supposed to go</i></strong><i> to the office today.</i></p> <p>Here, the person who speaks talks about a situation planned or arranged beforehand. However, it implies others&rsquo; expectation of his being at the office today.</p> <p><i>We<strong> are not supposed to </strong>download files from the servers. </i></p> <p>In this example, we talk about things that are forbidden, prohibited, or not advisable. At the end, you can perceive this expression as if someone wouldn&rsquo;t expect you to do a specific thing.</p> <p>Here you are the structure for this grammar point:</p> <p>Subject + <strong>verb to be</strong> + (<strong>not</strong>) + <strong>supposed</strong><strong>to</strong> + verb + complement</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "As you know, I've implemented cloud computing in my company; it's supposed to help a lot with our business and customers."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm supposed to know all about it but, what are the benefits of using cloud services?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "So, companies aren't supposed to increase their fees with this service. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Characteristics of Economies of Scale"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong>Economics of scale</strong> are achieved when a company grows, increases its production, and decreases its costs.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>There are different inputs and characteristics that result in the production of economies of scale.</p> <ul> <li>Lower input cost: When a company gets goods in bulk, organizations can take advantage of volume discounts.</li> <li>Costly inputs: Research, development, advertising, and others are expensive, but they can decrease costs when used efficiently.</li> <li>Specialized inputs: Specialized labor can benefit the production of the company. Workers who are qualified for specific jobs can result in great efficiency for companies.</li> <li>Techniques and organizational inputs: Organizational skill can be implemented to the company to improve its techniques for production.</li> <li>Learning inputs: The learning process can be linked to the production and the companies&rsquo; improvements.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Companies must be aware that</strong> the sources vary. They need to take decisions effectively to improve the organization&rsquo;s production and incomes. They just need to balance the effect of the decisions and the sources, for not affecting the costs.</p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "foremost"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something is the most important  in a group"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, first and foremost, cost saving."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cut down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to reduce the amount of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In this way, organizations cut down costs for salaries, office space, and the like."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "scalability"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability of growing or increasing something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Scalability is another important benefit."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "saving"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "quantity of money kept for a specific purpose"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Besides, savings are supposed to be made with economies of scale."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "robust"},